# 15. Quality & Integrity Requirements

1. Original engine results must remain preserved.
2. Normalization must be traceable.
3. Provenance must survive every transformation.
4. Engine-specific scoring systems must remain distinguishable.
5. Historical and current information must not be conflated.
6. Duplicate detection must not erase independent evidence.
7. Conflicts must not be silently resolved.
8. Missing information must remain explicitly missing.
9. Inferences must be distinguishable from sourced facts.
10. Partial results must retain their completion status.
11. Cross-engine reconciliation must respect data ownership.
12. Final responses must not introduce unsupported claims.
13. Privacy and authorization checks must apply throughout assembly.
14. The Orchestrator must not directly modify engine-owned records.

